ipe, each observation gets its own node, so the other copy's choice stays fixed when I intervene on mine. Working through the payoffs with p as the chance the other copy sends, quiet pays 2(1-p)+5p and sending pays 4p, so sending always comes out ahead. A-FDT as the essay describes it therefore says to send, though I'm wondering whether treating the two observations as the same function would change that.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working out how A-FDT applies here: the two copies see different observations, so each has its own node, and intervening on mine leaves the other's fixed, meaning its action won't follow mine, which points toward defecting.\n\nUnder the essay's recipe, each observation gets its own node, so the other copy's choice stays fixed when I intervene on mine. Working through the payoffs with p as the chance the other copy sends, quiet pays 2(1-p)+5p and sending pays 4p, so sending always comes out ahead. A-FDT as the essay describes it therefore says to send, though I'm wondering whether treating the two observations as the same function would change that.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9711,"completion_tokens":1071,"total_tokens":10782,"cost":0.060264,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.060264,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038844,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02142},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":582,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}